  "question": {
    "text": "A curve in the first quadrant is such that the slope of <math><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi></math> is twice the slope of the tangent drawn at <math><mi>P</mi></math> to the curve, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math> is the origin and <math><mi>P</mi></math> is any general point on the curve. If the curve passes through <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then its equation is"
